---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
---
<Base
  title={"About · NoCloudware"}
  description={"NoCloudware: independent software by Adrian Goodrich. Licensed once or free, with no subscriptions, monthly fees or pay-per-use."}
  ogImage={"https://www.nocloudware.com/ncw_logo_cloudy.webp"}
  ogType="website"
>
  <div class="legacy-main">
  <div class="container">
    <section style="max-width:750px;margin:0 auto;">
      <div style="text-align:center;margin-bottom:2rem;">
        <img src="/ncw_logo_cloudy.webp" alt="NoCloudware" class="product-logo-lg">
      </div>
      <h1>About NoCloudware</h1>
      <div class="mission-text">
        <p>NoCloudware started as a complaint. Software had quietly become rent: a monthly fee that never ends, or a meter that keeps spinning every time you use it. On top of that, most of it now wants an account, a subscription and a stack of credits before it does anything at all.</p>
        <p>The rule that came out of that complaint is simple: <strong>software you own</strong>. Pay once, or don't pay at all. No subscriptions, no freemium traps, no treating your data as the product.</p>
        <p>That rule is about <strong>licensing</strong>, not about infrastructure. NoCloudware has nothing against the cloud, and future products will use cloud hosting and storage. The difference is whose cloud it is: yours. It lives in your own account, you can keep it or take it anywhere, and NoCloudware neither administers it nor answers for it. Complete sovereignty over your own content, unless you bring us in to build custom features on top.</p>
        <p>Most of what exists here was born from an annoyance of my own, not from a feature roadmap. <strong>TurnAFile</strong> came first: I needed to convert files without depending on the internet, so I built it and didn't depend on the internet either. <strong>SigilForge</strong> answered a creative need and was given away free. <strong>PoleShift</strong> and <strong>TubeMassDL</strong> were built to do something real with no subscription or third-party service standing in the way. <strong>Bluesk-AI</strong> and <strong>Archivo de Miedos</strong> were experiments in building and sharing something without putting someone else's platform in the middle of it.</p>
        <p>A clear example of the model is a mail service I'm putting together on Cloudflare and Resend: completely free, hosted on your own Cloudflare account, your mail under your own sovereignty. NoCloudware steps in only for custom development, never as an administrator between you and your data.</p>
        <p>NoCloudware is a small independent studio, run by one person, that keeps to that rule: <strong>your license, your infrastructure, your data</strong>.</p>
      </div>

      <h2><Icon name="mail" /> Contact</h2>
      <p class="text-muted">For technical support, licensing questions or suggestions: <a href="mailto:nocloudware@outlook.com" style="color:var(--aether-accent);font-weight:600;">nocloudware@outlook.com</a></p>

      <h2><Icon name="money" /> Support the project</h2>
      <p class="text-muted">NoCloudware is an independent project by <strong>Adrian Goodrich</strong>. If you value software without subscriptions, consider supporting its development.</p>
      <div class="btn-group">
        <a class="btn btn-donate" href="/donate.html"> Support the project</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>

</Base>
